1 PETER 

CH5

14
Greet one another with a kiss of love. Peace be to you all who are in Christ.

13
She who is in Babylon chosen together with you sends you greetings and so does Mark my son.

12
Through Silvanus the faithful brother as I regard him I have written to you briefly exhorting and testifying that this is the true grace of God in which you stand.

11
To Him be dominion forever and ever. Amen.

10
And the God of all grace who called you to His eternal glory in Christ after you have suffered a little while will Himself perfect confirm strengthen and establish you.

9
Resist him firm in the faith knowing that the same experiences of suffering are being accomplished by your brotherhood in the world.

8
Be of sober spirit be on the alert your adversary the devil prowls around like a roaring lion seeking someone to devour.

7
Casting all your anxiety on Him because He cares for you.

6
Therefore humble yourselves under the mighty hand of God that He may exalt you at the proper time.

5
You younger men be subject to the elders and all of you clothe yourselves with humility toward one another for God is opposed to the proud but gives grace to the humble.

4
And when the Chief Shepherd appears you will receive the unfading crown of glory.

3
Not lording it over those allotted to your charge but being examples to the flock.

2
Shepherd the flock of God among you exercising oversight not under compulsion but willingly not for sordid gain but with eagerness.

1
Therefore I exhort the elders among you as a fellow elder and witness of the sufferings of Christ and a partaker also of the glory that is to be revealed.

CH4

19
Therefore let those who suffer according to the will of God entrust their souls to a faithful Creator in doing what is right.

18
And if the righteous is scarcely saved what will become of the ungodly and sinner.

17
For it is time for judgment to begin with the household of God and if it begins with us first what will be the end of those who do not obey the gospel of God.

16
But if anyone suffers as a Christian let him not be ashamed but let him glorify God in this name.

15
Let none of you suffer as a murderer or a thief or an evildoer or as a meddler in other men’s matters.

14
If you are reviled for the name of Christ you are blessed because the Spirit of glory and of God rests upon you.

13
But to the degree that you share the sufferings of Christ keep on rejoicing so that also at the revelation of His glory you may rejoice with exultation.

12
Beloved do not be surprised at the fiery ordeal among you which comes upon you for your testing as though a strange thing were happening to you.

11
If anyone speaks as one who is speaking the oracles of God if anyone serves as one who is serving by the strength which God supplies so that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ to whom belongs the glory and dominion forever and ever. Amen.

10
As each one has received a special gift employ it in serving one another as good stewards of the manifold grace of God.

9
Be hospitable to one another without grumbling.

8
Above all keep fervent in your love for one another because love covers a multitude of sins.

7
The end of all things is near therefore be of sound judgment and sober spirit for the purpose of prayer.

6
For the gospel was preached even to those who are dead so that though judged in the flesh according to men they might live according to God in the spirit.

5
They will give an account to Him who is ready to judge the living and the dead.

4
They think it strange that you do not run with them into the same excess of dissipation and they malign you.

3
For the time already past is sufficient for you to have carried out the desire of the Gentiles having pursued a course of sensuality in drunkenness carousals drinking parties and abominable idolatries.

2
So as to no longer live the rest of the time in the flesh for the lusts of men but for the will of God.

1
Therefore since Christ has suffered in the flesh arm yourselves also with the same purpose because he who has suffered in the flesh has ceased from sin.

CH3

22
Who is at the right hand of God having gone into heaven after angels and authorities and powers had been subjected to Him.

21
Corresponding to that baptism now saves you not the removal of dirt from the flesh but an appeal to God for a good conscience through the resurrection of Jesus Christ.

20
Who once were disobedient when the patience of God waited in the days of Noah during the construction of the ark in which a few that is eight persons were brought safely through the water.

19
In which also He went and made proclamation to the spirits now in prison.

18
For Christ also suffered for sins once for all the just for the unjust so that He might bring us to God having been put to death in the flesh but made alive in the spirit.

17
For it is better if the will of God should desire it that you suffer for doing what is right rather than for doing what is wrong.

16
But if anyone suffers as a Christian let him not be ashamed but let him glorify God in this name.

15
But sanctify Christ as Lord in your hearts always being ready to make a defense to everyone who asks you for an account concerning the hope that is in you yet with gentleness and fear.

14
But even if you should suffer for the sake of righteousness you are blessed and do not fear their intimidation and do not be troubled.

13
And who is there to harm you if you become zealous for what is good.

12
For the eyes of the Lord are on the righteous and His ears are open to their prayer but the face of the Lord is against those who do evil.

11
Let him turn away from evil and do good. Let him seek peace and pursue it.

10
For the one who desires life and to see good days let him keep his tongue from evil and his lips from speaking deceit.

9
Do not return evil for evil or insult for insult but giving a blessing instead for you were called for this purpose that you might inherit a blessing.

8
To sum up all of you be harmonious, sympathetic, brotherly, kindhearted, and humble in spirit.

7
You husbands likewise live with your wives in an understanding way as with a weaker vessel since she is a woman and show her honor as a fellow heir of the grace of life so that your prayers will not be hindered.

6
As Sarah obeyed Abraham calling him lord whose children you have become if you do what is right and do not fear any intimidation.

5
For in this way in former times the holy women also who hoped in God used to adorn themselves being submissive to their own husbands.

4
But let it be the hidden person of the heart with the imperishable beauty of a gentle and quiet spirit which is precious in the sight of God.

3
Let not your adornment be merely external braiding of hair and wearing gold jewelry or putting on fine clothing.

2
As they observe your chaste and respectful behavior.

1
In the same way you wives be submissive to your own husbands so that even if any of them are disobedient to the word they may be won without a word by the behavior of their wives.

CH2

25
For you were straying like sheep but now you have returned to the Shepherd and Guardian of your souls.

24
Who Himself bore our sins in His body on the cross so that we might die to sin and live to righteousness by whose wounds you were healed.

23
While being reviled He did not revile in return while suffering He uttered no threats but kept entrusting Himself to Him who judges righteously.

22
Who committed no sin nor was deceit found in His mouth.

21
For you have been called for this purpose since Christ also suffered for you leaving you an example so that you might follow in His steps.

20
For what credit is there if when you sin and are harshly treated you endure it with patience but if when you do what is right and suffer for it you patiently endure this finds favor with God.

19
For this is grace if for the sake of conscience toward God a person bears up under sorrows when suffering unjustly.

18
Servants be submissive to your masters with all respect not only to those who are good and gentle but also to those who are unreasonable.

17
Honor all people love the brotherhood fear God honor the king.

16
As free men and not using your freedom as a covering for evil but as bondslaves of God.

15
For such is the will of God that by doing right you may silence the ignorance of foolish men.

14
Whether to the king as supreme or to governors as sent by him for the punishment of evildoers and the praise of those who do right.

13
Submit yourselves for the Lord’s sake to every human institution whether to a king as the one in authority or to governors as sent by him.

12
Keep your behavior excellent among the Gentiles so that in the thing in which they slander you as evildoers they may because of your good deeds as they observe them glorify God in the day of visitation.

11
Beloved I urge you as aliens and strangers to abstain from fleshly lusts which wage war against the soul.

10
Who once were not a people but now are the people of God who had not received mercy but now have received mercy.

9
But you are a chosen race a royal priesthood a holy nation a people for God’s own possession so that you may proclaim the excellencies of Him who has called you out of darkness into His marvelous light.

8
A stone of stumbling and a rock of offense for they stumble because they are disobedient to the word to this doom they were also appointed.

7
This precious value is for you who believe but for those who disbelieve the stone which the builders rejected this became the chief cornerstone.

6
For it is contained in Scripture: Behold I lay in Zion a choice stone a precious cornerstone and he who believes in Him will not be disappointed.

5
You also as living stones are being built up as a spiritual house for a holy priesthood to offer up spiritual sacrifices acceptable to God through Jesus Christ.

4
And coming to Him as to a living stone rejected by men but chosen and precious in the sight of God.

3
If you have tasted that the Lord is good.

2
Like newborn babies long for the pure milk of the word so that by it you may grow in respect to salvation.

1
Therefore putting aside all malice and all deceit and hypocrisy and envy and all slander.

CH1

25
But the word of the Lord endures forever and this is the word which was preached to you.

24
For all flesh is like grass and all its glory like the flower of grass. The grass withers and the flower falls off.

23
Having been born again not of perishable seed but imperishable through the living and enduring word of God.

22
Having purified your souls in obedience to the truth through the Spirit for a sincere brotherly love love one another fervently from the heart.

21
Who through Him are believers in God who raised Him from the dead and gave Him glory so that your faith and hope are in God.

20
Who was foreknown before the foundation of the world but has appeared in these last times for your sake.

19
But with precious blood as of a lamb unblemished and spotless the blood of Christ.

18
Knowing that you were not redeemed with perishable things like silver or gold from your futile way of life inherited from your forefathers.

17
If you address as Father the One who impartially judges according to each one’s work conduct yourselves in fear during the time of your stay on earth.

16
Because it is written you shall be holy for I am holy.

15
But like the Holy One who called you be holy yourselves also in all your behavior.

14
As obedient children do not be conformed to the former lusts which were yours in your ignorance.

13
Therefore prepare your minds for action keep sober in spirit fix your hope completely on the grace to be brought to you at the revelation of Jesus Christ.

12
To whom it was revealed that they were not serving themselves but you in these things which have now been announced to you through those who preached the gospel to you by the Holy Spirit sent from heaven things into which angels long to look.

11
Seeking to know what person or time the Spirit of Christ within them was indicating as He predicted the sufferings of Christ and the glories to follow.

10
As to which salvation the prophets who prophesied of the grace that would come to you made careful search and inquiry.

9
Obtaining as the outcome of your faith the salvation of your souls.

8
Whom having not seen you love and though not seeing now but believing you greatly rejoice with joy inexpressible and full of glory.

7
So that the proof of your faith being more precious than gold which is perishable though tested by fire may be found to result in praise and glory and honor at the revelation of Jesus Christ.

6
In which you greatly rejoice even though now for a little while if necessary you have been distressed by various trials.

5
Who are protected by the power of God through faith for a salvation ready to be revealed in the last time.

4
Into an inheritance that is imperishable and undefiled and will not fade away reserved in heaven for you.

3
Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ who according to His great mercy has caused us to be born again to a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead.

2
According to the foreknowledge of God the Father by the sanctifying work of the Spirit to obey Jesus Christ and be sprinkled with His blood grace and peace be multiplied to you.

1
Peter an apostle of Jesus Christ to those who reside as aliens scattered throughout Pontus Galatia Cappadocia Asia and Bithynia.
